{"title":"2003 CEMC Galois Problems/Problem 1b","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Modular_Arithmetic)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Modular Arithmetic)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2003 CEMC Galois Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Show that the sum of the squares of any 5 consecutive integers is divisible by 5.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Like in solutions 1-3 of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1a\" title=\"2003 CEMC Galois Problems/Problem 1a\">part a</a>, we can make <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> one of the five numbers, and we can get one of these expressions as the sum of the squares depending on what number we made <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/0/4a060d894ba57cb9c1ec6c3138f81af9db2e587e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x^{2} + 20x + 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"120\" height=\"18\" /> (if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is the smallest number)\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/1/ef107e90f298ab84edd315e79c6bc5327adb9776.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x^{2} + 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" /> (if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is the middle number)\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/6/a2662d64d61b04475c87979fea12e95016b4e2c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x^{2} - 20x - 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"120\" height=\"18\" /> (if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is the largest number)\n</p><p>In all of these, we can realize that all of these factor with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/e/edee5bde1a7c76af3d2982a9e494ecb3d4dcb903.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x^{2} + 20x + 30 = 5(x^{2} + 4x + 6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"258\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/7/ad7bd4b38ebc402e4d6551939b10cd965b620f2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x^{2} + 10 = 5(x^{2} + 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"166\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/b/1bb200e7ea78d7479256c50c60138f1c92cea14e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x^{2} - 20x - 30 = 5(x^{2} - 4x + 6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"258\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> must be an integer, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/d/b4d536c1e6842465ee993939bf301166f1447bd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2} + 4x + 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"93\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/c/08c5e9a6ebc8712dd09028cba2788920c434b9d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2} + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/7/7570809f4ad237bda8320d1ee6198179ef5559d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2} - 4x + 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"93\" height=\"18\" /> must all be integers. Since we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times some integer, the result must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, the sum of the squares of any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> consecutive integers must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Modular_Arithmetic.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Modular_Arithmetic)\">Solution 2 (Modular Arithmetic)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Modular Arithmetic)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the first number of the five consecutive integers. Since the integers are consecutive, the list of numbers must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/d/9edc688e33895bf81c1b912055950d33a03e375a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, x + 1, x + 2, x + 3, x + 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"211\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>We can split into different cases based on what <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is. \n</p><p>First, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/4/ed4176572d045799a525c46fb658dfb7e3dae8e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\equiv 0 \\pmod{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"118\" height=\"20\" />, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/b/e6b6d63a520ed49cbd8bbe45d79a4307d7c6865b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 1 \\equiv 1 \\pmod {5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"149\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/8/248c5cdf2c8332f5632dfd260b8d35ee7a90f85b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 2 \\equiv 2 \\pmod {5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"149\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/e/33e8695f1953194d3518b1f629a231bba254b11b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 3 \\equiv 3 \\pmod {5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"149\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/5/6957fd0ce36197d8464be9df796f66a55d2f2a96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 4 \\equiv 4 \\pmod{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"149\" height=\"20\" />. We then have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/1/29176102a785ade767e9e28c8c7b953da1e10a77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2} + (x + 1)^{2} + (x + 2)^{2} + (x + 3)^{2} + (x + 4)^{2} \\equiv 0^{2} + 1^{2} + 2^{2} + 3^{2} + 4^{2} \\pmod{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"630\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/1/d61dbecfe61ae86cee4a662c23bca5a6b6db6425.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\equiv 0 + 1 + 2 + 3 + 4 \\pmod{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"228\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/4/8f45ecea66a0e777f3780164feea3ae91416f422.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\equiv 10 \\pmod{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"111\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/d/bdd7487abd388496dc431eca07e427e0db83a3cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\equiv 0 \\pmod{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"102\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Since this is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the sum of the squares must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Next, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/3/9733ce27586d2b9084e65e26c6be63419fb07f16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\equiv 1 \\pmod{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"118\" height=\"20\" />, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/3/7e399737a7700ac6ff9a916749ca31cd31df9d56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 1 \\equiv 2 \\pmod {5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"149\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/e/90ed5a7a8c45121a0c73ae31a4f2d32e55a00132.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 2 \\equiv 3 \\pmod {5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"149\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/0/b40f06acbe74c6d396812ebc90afdf73ec6d686a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 3 \\equiv 4 \\pmod {5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"149\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/e/74e8544f726cbe36622c249eaa09494acec9c503.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 4 \\equiv 5 \\pmod{5} \\equiv 0 \\pmod{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"255\" height=\"20\" />. However, we see that this will just have the same result as our previous case because the different results here are just switched around. This will also be true for the later cases since  mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> just cycles through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, for any five consecutive numbers, the sum of their squares must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017202317\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.020 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.036 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 189/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 78/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8331/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.823      1 2003_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1\n100.00%    5.823      1 -total\n-->\n